     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (850 mg TID) for immediate-release metformin. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** This could be 850 mg PO BID with meals, or 500 mg PO TID with meals if you want a dose that divides evenly.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf 1,700 mg TID really is what you want, please confirm. Include the clinical rationale if you want it in the order note. I'll enter the order once you reply."
      }
     ],
